## 4. Boot attempt — three hypotheses, no boot

H1 — Akuma KVM, the plan's own rig: `herd vm-run /root/denver/w/vm.spec`

```
[vm-run] no /dev/kvm0: the kernel was not booted with kvmctl
```

herd's vm_run does open("/dev/kvm0", O_RDWR) and the open failed. Precedent: docs/reference/
subsystems/kvm.md line 192 — "`ls /dev` does not list it; `open` is `ENOENT` unless the kernel
was booted with `kvmctl`" — and amd64/src/main.rs:334-348: the SVM hypervisor arms only on the
`kvmctl` (or `kvmtest`) boot flag. The CURRENT host boot (`Akuma akuma-ryzen 0.0.9
886dabf-release-smp-shared`) carries no such flag. There is no runtime arm.

H2 — Firecracker (present: /root/fc/firecracker, and /root/fc/run.sh shows the working form):
needs the same KVM device; docs/archive/AKUMA_FIRECRACKER_KVM.md — same `kvmctl`-armed boot
required. Dead for the same reason.

H3 — plain QEMU: no qemu-system binary anywhere on the box (/usr/local, /opt incl. the gentoo
root at /opt/gentoo/root, /root). Nothing to run even TCG with.

Per the runbook: the stall protocol's remedy (insert a diagnostic pass) does not apply — the
diagnostic already exists and names the exact missing thing: a reboot with `kvmctl kvmmem=4096`
on the host command line (kvm.md entry 30, 2026-10-22). A reboot is beyond this plan's authority
and would kill the session running on the machine. Escape hatch: denver/ESCALATE.md.

RESULT FAIL: no /dev/kvm0 — host not booted with kvmctl; scaffold + build complete and captured
above; boot probe pending the host reboot. This file must gain a RESULT PASS line from the
